function renderDepartments(){
 $('page-departments').innerHTML=`<div class="page-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">YOUR WORKFORCE</div><h1>Departments & populations</h1><p class="sub">Your populations, annual attrition and learning capacity.</p></div><div class="actions"><button id="csv-export">Export department CSV</button><label class="button">Import department CSV<input type="file" accept=".csv,text/csv" id="csv-import" hidden></label><button id="add-dept">Add department</button><button id="population-backup">Export previous setup</button></div></div><div class="notice">Your six population names and annual attrition rates are prefilled. Enter actual starting headcounts, expected joiners and learning capacity; zero means no associates or capacity, not an estimate. If using a closed cohort, also assign its places in Programme. Some groups overlap: use one population or non-overlapping groups. Previous settings are recoverable using Export previous setup. Historical programme totals below are reference data and do not calibrate forecasts.</div><form id="departments-form"><div class="editor-grid">${scenario.departments.map((d,i)=>`<section class="panel dept-item"><div class="row"><h2>${esc(d.name)}</h2><button type="button" data-remove="${i}" ${scenario.departments.length===1?'disabled':''}>Remove</button></div><div class="form-grid">${field('Department name',`d${i}-name`,d.name,{type:'text',full:true})}${deptFields.map(([label,k,max,step])=>field(k==='headcount'&&d.headcountBasis==='cohort'?'Starting associates · cohort only':label,`d${i}-${k}`,d[k],{max,step})).join('')}${d.headcountBasis==='cohort'?`<label class="toggle full"><span>This headcount is now the full population total</span><input type="checkbox" name="d${i}-fullHeadcount"></label><p class="form-hint">Currently models only your selected cohort. Enter the full population count and tick this option when it is known.</p>`:''}</div><details><summary>Archetype mix · must total 100%</summary><div class="form-grid">${scenario.archetypes.map((a,j)=>field(esc(a.name)+' (%)',`d${i}-mix${j}`,d.mix[j],{max:100,step:.1})).join('')}</div></details><details><summary>Historical programme reference</summary><p class="form-hint">Totals from one comparable programme, with matching invitation and completion windows. No individual employee records are stored.</p><div class="form-grid">${[['Invited','historyInvited'],['Started','historyStarted'],['Completed','historyCompleted']].map(([label,k])=>field(label,`d${i}-${k}`,d[k],{max:100000})).join('')}</div></details><details><summary>Monthly joiners and leavers · override annual estimates</summary><p class="form-hint">Blank uses the annual estimate. Zero explicitly means none. Departures happen before arrivals each month. Figures entered here replace—not add to—the annual assumptions for that month.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table class="schedule"><thead><tr><th>Month</th><th>Joiners</th><th>Leavers</th></tr></thead><tbody>${Array.from({length:24},(_,j)=>{let v=d.schedule[j+1]||{};return `<tr><td>${esc(M.monthLabel(scenario,j+1))}</td><td><input aria-label="${esc(d.name)} joiners month ${j+1}" type="number" min="0" max="2000" step="1" name="d${i}-join${j+1}" value="${v.join??''}" placeholder="Auto"></td><td><input aria-label="${esc(d.name)} leavers month ${j+1}" type="number" min="0" max="2000" step="1" name="d${i}-leave${j+1}" value="${v.leave??''}" placeholder="Auto"></td></tr>`}).join('')}</tbody></table></div></details></section>`).join('')}</div><div class="form-actions"><button class="primary" type="submit">Save departments & update simulation</button><span class="small muted">Edits apply when you save.</span></div></form>`;
 document.querySelectorAll('.dept-item').forEach((el,i)=>el.querySelector('.form-grid').insertAdjacentHTML('afterend','<details><summary>Seniority mix · separate from archetypes</summary><p class="form-hint">Percentages must total 100. Unknown data stays Not specified. This mix is used for current associates and new joiners.</p><div class="form-grid">'+M.seniorityLevels(scenario).map((v,j)=>field(esc(v.name)+' (%)','d'+i+'-seniority'+j,M.seniorityMix(scenario.departments[i])[j],{max:100,step:.1})).join('')+'</div></details>'));
 $('population-backup').hidden=!scenario.populationSetupBackup;$('population-backup').onclick=()=>download('learning-lab-previous-setup.json',JSON.stringify({...scenario.populationSetupBackup,populationDepartmentsVersion:1},null,2));
 $('departments-form').onsubmit=e=>{e.preventDefault();try{const draft=M.clone(scenario),f=new FormData(e.target);draft.departments.forEach((d,i)=>{d.name=f.get(`d${i}-name`).trim();if(f.has(`d${i}-fullHeadcount`))delete d.headcountBasis;for(const [,k]of deptFields)d[k]=+f.get(`d${i}-${k}`);for(const k of ['historyInvited','historyStarted','historyCompleted'])d[k]=+f.get(`d${i}-${k}`);d.mix=d.mix.map((_,j)=>+f.get(`d${i}-mix${j}`));d.seniorityMix=M.seniorityLevels(draft).map((_,j)=>+f.get(`d${i}-seniority${j}`));d.schedule={};for(let m=1;m<=24;m++){let o={};for(const k of ['join','leave']){let v=f.get(`d${i}-${k}${m}`);if(v!=='')o[k]=+v;}if(Object.keys(o).length)d.schedule[m]=o}});applyDraft(draft,'Departments saved. Workforce and both learning plans have been updated.');renderDepartments();}catch(err){notify('Changes not applied: '+err.message)}};
 $('add-dept').onclick=()=>{try{const draft=readDepartmentDraft();let n=1;while(draft.departments.some(d=>d.id==='department-'+n))n++;draft.departments.push({...M.clone(M.DEFAULT.departments[0]),id:'department-'+n,name:'New department '+n,headcount:30,hires:6,schedule:{},historyInvited:0,historyStarted:0,historyCompleted:0});applyDraft(draft,'Department added. Edit its sample assumptions and save.');renderDepartments()}catch(e){notify(e.message)}};
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-remove]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{try{const draft=readDepartmentDraft();draft.departments.splice(+b.dataset.remove,1);applyDraft(draft,'Department removed from this scenario.');renderDepartments()}catch(e){notify(e.message)}});
 $('csv-export').onclick=()=>exportDepartments();$('csv-import').onchange=importDepartments;
}
function readDepartmentDraft(){const form=$('departments-form'),f=new FormData(form),draft=M.clone(scenario);if(!form.reportValidity())throw Error('Check the highlighted field before continuing.');draft.departments.forEach((d,i)=>{d.name=f.get(`d${i}-name`).trim();if(f.has(`d${i}-fullHeadcount`))delete d.headcountBasis;for(const [,k]of deptFields)d[k]=+f.get(`d${i}-${k}`);for(const k of ['historyInvited','historyStarted','historyCompleted'])d[k]=+f.get(`d${i}-${k}`);d.mix=d.mix.map((_,j)=>+f.get(`d${i}-mix${j}`));d.seniorityMix=M.seniorityLevels(draft).map((_,j)=>+f.get(`d${i}-seniority${j}`));d.schedule={};for(let m=1;m<=24;m++){const o={};for(const k of ['join','leave'])if(f.get(`d${i}-${k}${m}`)!=='')o[k]=+f.get(`d${i}-${k}${m}`);if(Object.keys(o).length)d.schedule[m]=o}});M.validate(draft);return draft}
const csvHeaders=['id','name','headcount','hires','turnover','mandatoryHours','mandatoryDone','capacity','onboarding','mix1','mix2','mix3','mix4','historyInvited','historyStarted','historyCompleted'];
function exportDepartments(){try{const draft=readDepartmentDraft(),quote=v=>'"'+String(v).replace(/"/g,'""')+'"';download('learning-lab-departments.csv',[csvHeaders.join(','),...draft.departments.map(d=>csvHeaders.map(k=>quote(k.startsWith('mix')?d.mix[+k.slice(3)-1]:d[k])).join(','))].join('\r\n'),'text/csv');notify('CSV exported. Monthly overrides are only included in the full scenario JSON export.')}catch(e){notify(e.message)}}
function parseCSV(text){let rows=[],row=[],v='',quoted=false;for(let i=0;i<text.length;i++){const c=text[i];if(c==='"'){if(quoted&&text[i+1]==='"'){v+='"';i++}else quoted=!quoted}else if(c===','&&!quoted){row.push(v);v=''}else if((c==='\n'||c==='\r')&&!quoted){if(c==='\r'&&text[i+1]==='\n')i++;row.push(v);if(row.some(x=>x.trim()))rows.push(row);row=[];v=''}else v+=c}if(quoted)throw Error('Unclosed quote in CSV.');if(v||row.length){row.push(v);rows.push(row)}return rows}
async function importDepartments(e){let file=e.target.files[0];if(!file)return;try{if(file.size>2000000)throw Error('CSV must be below 2 MB.');const rows=parseCSV((await file.text()).replace(/^\uFEFF/,'')),header=rows.shift()?.map(x=>x.trim());if(!header||csvHeaders.some(k=>!header.includes(k)))throw Error('Use the column names in Export department CSV.');const draft=M.clone(scenario);draft.departments=rows.map((row,i)=>{if(row.length!==header.length)throw Error('CSV row '+(i+2)+' has a different number of columns.');const o=Object.fromEntries(header.map((k,j)=>[k,row[j].trim()]));const d={id:o.id,name:o.name,cohortSize:scenario.departments.find(d=>d.id===o.id)?.cohortSize,seniorityMix:M.clone(M.seniorityMix(scenario.departments.find(d=>d.id===o.id)||{})),schedule:M.clone(scenario.departments.find(d=>d.id===o.id)?.schedule||{}),mix:[]};for(const k of csvHeaders){if(k==='id'||k==='name')continue;if(o[k]==='')throw Error('Missing '+k+' on row '+(i+2));if(k.startsWith('mix'))d.mix.push(Number(o[k]));else d[k]=Number(o[k])}return d});applyDraft(draft,'Department CSV imported. Matching department IDs retain their monthly workforce overrides.');renderDepartments()}catch(err){notify('CSV not imported: '+err.message)}e.target.value=''}
function renderPersonas(){
 $('page-personas').innerHTML=`<div class="page-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">BEHAVIOURAL ASSUMPTIONS</div><h1>Archetypes, not stereotypes.</h1><p class="sub">Define how fictional groups engage with learning.</p></div></div><div class="notice">These are editable assumptions, not measured employee traits. Department percentages determine the expected mix; each simulated person is sampled from that mix.</div><form id="personas-form"><div class="editor-grid">${scenario.archetypes.map((a,i)=>`<section class="panel"><h2><i class="key" style="background:${a.color}"></i>${esc(a.name)}</h2><div class="form-grid">${field('Archetype name',`a${i}-name`,a.name,{type:'text',full:true})}${field('Monthly opening chance (%)',`a${i}-open`,a.open,{max:100,hint:'Before sponsor and manager effects.'})}${field('Monthly start chance once opened (%)',`a${i}-start`,a.start,{max:100,hint:'Requires time left after existing training.'})}${field('Available-time engagement (%)',`a${i}-engagement`,a.engagement,{max:100,hint:'Share of remaining learning time used, before modifiers.'})}${field('Manager effect on starting (percentage points)',`a${i}-manager`,a.manager,{max:100})}<label>Archetype colour<input type="color" name="a${i}-color" value="${a.color}"></label></div></section>`).join('')}</div><div class="form-actions"><button type="submit" class="primary">Save archetypes & update simulation</button></div></form>`;
 $('personas-form').querySelector('.form-actions').insertAdjacentHTML('beforebegin','<section class="panel" style="margin-top:20px"><h2>Seniority & classroom willingness</h2><p class="small muted">Seniority is independent of learning archetype. Neutral defaults avoid assuming that senior associates are less willing. These optional effects adjust the monthly chance of starting classroom learning, in percentage points; they do not affect self-paced learning.</p><div class="form-grid">'+M.seniorityLevels(scenario).slice(1).map((v,i)=>field(esc(v.name)+' · classroom effect (pp)','seniority-effect'+(i+1),v.classroomEffect,{min:-50,max:50})).join('')+'</div><p class="form-hint">For example, −10 means ten percentage points lower starting probability. Treat this as a hypothesis until you have evidence. Not specified always has zero effect.</p></section>');
 $('personas-form').onsubmit=e=>{e.preventDefault();try{const draft=M.clone(scenario),f=new FormData(e.target);draft.archetypes.forEach((a,i)=>{a.name=f.get(`a${i}-name`).trim();a.color=f.get(`a${i}-color`);for(const k of ['open','start','engagement','manager'])a[k]=+f.get(`a${i}-${k}`)});draft.seniority=M.clone(M.seniorityLevels(scenario));draft.seniority.forEach((v,i)=>{v.classroomEffect=i?+f.get('seniority-effect'+i):0});applyDraft(draft,'Archetypes and seniority assumptions saved.');renderPersonas()}catch(err){notify('Changes not applied: '+err.message)}};
}
function renderProgramme(){const p=scenario.programme,c=p.baseline;
 $('page-programme').innerHTML=`<div class="page-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">LEARNING DESIGN</div><h1>The programme & its context.</h1><p class="sub">One proposed programme, alongside existing mandatory learning.</p></div></div><form id="programme-form"><div class="editor-grid"><section class="panel"><h2>Programme</h2><div class="form-grid">${field('Programme name','name',p.name,{type:'text',full:true})}${field('Total learning hours','hours',p.hours,{min:.5,max:200,step:.5})}${field('Number of modules','modules',p.modules,{min:1,max:50})}${field('Launch month in simulation','launch',p.launch,{min:1,max:24})}${field('Completion window from assignment (months)','deadline',p.deadline,{min:1,max:24})}<label>Audience<select name="audience"><option value="all" ${p.audience==='all'?'selected':''}>Current associates and new joiners</option><option value="existing" ${p.audience==='existing'?'selected':''}>Current associates only — closed cohort</option><option value="joiners" ${p.audience==='joiners'?'selected':''}>New joiners only</option></select></label></div><p class="form-hint">Current associates means those present at the simulation start. That closed cohort excludes all later joiners, including arrivals before a delayed course launch. Leavers remain visible in historical results. Open audiences add eligible new joiners.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Baseline plan A</h2><div class="form-grid">${['sponsor','manager','mandatory'].map((k,i)=>`<label class="toggle full"><span>${['Active sponsor','Manager encouragement','Mandatory programme'][i]}</span><input type="checkbox" name="${k}" ${c[k]?'checked':''}></label>`).join('')}${field('Extra protected hours / month','protected',c.protected,{max:8,step:.5})}${field('Relevance (1–5)','relevance',c.relevance,{min:1,max:5})}</div><p class="form-hint">Protected hours are added to each department’s regular learning capacity. Plan B is edited on the Simulation screen.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Scenario settings</h2><div class="form-grid">${field('Scenario name','scenarioName',scenario.name,{type:'text',full:true})}<label>Start month<input type="month" name="startMonth" min="2000-01" max="2099-12" value="${scenario.start}" required></label>${field('Population seed','seed',scenario.seed,{min:1,max:100000})}</div><p class="form-hint">The seed makes runs repeatable. Start month controls calendar labels and the first year’s remaining mandatory hours.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Mandatory workload by calendar month</h2><p class="form-hint">Weights distribute annual mandatory hours. A weight of 2 assigns twice as many hours as 1. Weights are normalised; they never increase the annual total.</p><div class="form-grid">${scenario.seasonal.map((n,i)=>field(new Date(2027,i,1).toLocaleDateString('en-GB',{month:'long'}),'season'+i,n,{min:.1,max:3,step:.1})).join('')}</div></section></div><div class="form-actions"><button type="submit" class="primary">Save programme & update simulation</button></div></form>`;
 $('programme-form').querySelector('.form-actions').insertAdjacentHTML('beforebegin',profileEditor(p.profile||{}));
 $('programme-form').querySelector('select[name="audience"]').closest('.panel').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend','<section id="cohort-editor" style="margin-top:20px"><h3>Closed cohort places</h3><p class="form-hint">Enter how many current associates are selected from each department. For a 50-person programme, distribute 50 places across the rows. Enter zero for populations outside the cohort. When the full headcount is unknown, enter the selected cohort directly: those associates become the simulated starting population, labelled Cohort only. Known full headcounts remain unchanged.</p><div class="form-grid">'+scenario.departments.map((d,i)=>field(esc(d.name)+(d.headcount===0||d.headcountBasis==='cohort'?' · enter selected associates':' · up to '+d.headcount),'cohort'+i,d.cohortSize??d.headcount,{max:M.cohortInputLimit(d),hint:d.headcount===0||d.headcountBasis==='cohort'?'Full population headcount unknown. Entering 50 models those 50 selected associates only.':''})).join('')+'</div><p id="cohort-total" role="status" style="margin-top:12px"></p><p class="form-hint">Places select a repeatable sample using the department’s archetype and seniority mix. This is not an import of named associates.</p></section>');
 const updateCohort=()=>{const enabled=$('programme-form').elements.audience.value==='existing';$('cohort-editor').hidden=!enabled;const inputs=Array.from($('cohort-editor').querySelectorAll('input'));inputs.forEach(input=>input.disabled=!enabled);$('cohort-total').textContent='Total selected: '+inputs.reduce((total,input)=>total+(Number(input.value)||0),0)+' associates';};
 $('programme-form').elements.audience.addEventListener('change',updateCohort);$('cohort-editor').addEventListener('input',updateCohort);updateCohort();
 $('programme-form').querySelector('select[name="audience"]').closest('label').insertAdjacentHTML('afterend','<label>Delivery format<select name="delivery"><option value="self-paced">Self-paced learning</option><option value="classroom">Classroom / instructor-led</option></select><span class="form-hint">Classroom willingness by seniority is adjustable under Archetypes. Session dates, seats and actual attendance are not modelled.</span></label>');$('programme-form').elements.delivery.value=p.delivery||'self-paced';
 $('programme-form').onsubmit=e=>{e.preventDefault();try{let draft=M.clone(scenario);const f=new FormData(e.target);draft.name=f.get('scenarioName').trim();draft.start=f.get('startMonth');draft.seed=+f.get('seed');draft.programme.name=f.get('name').trim();draft.programme.audience=f.get('audience');if(draft.programme.audience==='existing')draft.departments.forEach((d,i)=>d.cohortSize=+f.get('cohort'+i));draft.programme.delivery=f.get('delivery');for(const k of ['hours','modules','launch','deadline'])draft.programme[k]=+f.get(k);for(const k of ['sponsor','manager','mandatory'])draft.programme.baseline[k]=f.has(k);for(const k of ['protected','relevance'])draft.programme.baseline[k]=+f.get(k);draft.seasonal=draft.seasonal.map((_,i)=>+f.get('season'+i));draft.programme.profile=Object.fromEntries(PROFILE_FIELDS.map(([key])=>[key,String(f.get('profile-'+key)||'').trim()]));if(draft.programme.audience==='existing')draft=M.setCohortAllocations(draft,draft.departments.map(d=>d.cohortSize));applyDraft(draft,'Programme, strategic profile and baseline saved.');renderProgramme()}catch(err){notify('Changes not applied: '+err.message)}};
}
const PROFILE_FIELDS=[
 ['strategyAlignment','Strategy alignment',['Low — core functional / divisional','Medium — cross-segment / functional strategic','High — Digital / Leadership / Sales'],'Programme priority under your supplied rubric; this is not employee-perceived relevance.'],
 ['businessOutcomes','Intended business outcomes',null,'Describe the intended revenue, productivity, risk, skills or knowledge outcome. Intended impact is not measured impact.'],
 ['reach','Intended reach & visibility',['Low — fewer than 500','Medium — 500 to 5,000','High — more than 5,000'],'Organisation-wide scope. Actual simulated audience comes from Departments and the programme audience.'],
 ['skillBuilding','Required level of learning',['1 — Knowledge','2 — Skills','3 — Behaviour','4 — Performance'],'Completion alone cannot demonstrate behaviour change or business performance.'],
 ['signatureProcess','Signature process',['Low — industry-wide','Medium — organisation-specific version','High — core organisational practice'],'Importance to distinctive operations and culture.'],
 ['bespokeness','Bespokeness',['Low — mostly industry content','Medium — an organisation-specific approach','High — fully custom ways of working / process'],'Content development needs; custom content is not assumed to improve uptake.'],
 ['preparedness','Preparedness',['Early — key inputs not yet defined','Partial — some inputs ready','Ready — objectives and content reviewed; vendor arranged if needed'],'Capture readiness; any effects on launch timing or quality remain hypotheses.'],
 ['investmentLevel','Investment level',['Low — below $50k','Medium — $50k to $300k','High — above $300k'],'Development, resources and technology investment. No automatic participation effect.'],
 ['changeImpact','Change impact / deployment needs',['Low','Medium','High'],'Required implementation support, not evidence that support has been provided.'],
 ['stakeholders','Stakeholders & commitment',null,'Record stakeholder numbers, seniority, SMEs, commitment and unresolved approvals separately in your notes.']
];
function profileEditor(profile){return `<section class="panel" style="margin-top:20px"><div class="row"><h2>Strategic impact & delivery profile</h2><span class="badge">Context only · not a prediction score</span></div><p class="small muted" style="margin-top:10px">Your programme evaluation framework, kept alongside the simulation. These fields are saved and exported but do not change completion probabilities.</p><div class="form-grid">${PROFILE_FIELDS.map(([key,label,options,hint])=>`<label>${label}${options?`<select name="profile-${key}"><option value="">Not assessed</option>${options.map(v=>`<option value="${esc(v)}" ${profile[key]===v?'selected':''}>${esc(v)}</option>`).join('')}</select>`:`<textarea name="profile-${key}" rows="3" maxlength="2000">${esc(profile[key]||'')}</textarea>`}<span class="form-hint">${hint}</span></label>`).join('')}</div><p class="form-hint" style="margin-top:18px">Total impact is not calculated: scoring weights and aggregation rules have not been provided. High strategic value can coexist with low participation; high complexity can increase the support required.</p></section>`}
function renderMethod(){const rows=scenario.departments.map(d=>`<tr><td>${esc(d.name)}</td><td>${d.historyInvited}</td><td>${d.historyStarted}</td><td>${d.historyCompleted}</td><td>${d.historyInvited?Math.round(d.historyCompleted/d.historyInvited*100)+'%':'—'}</td></tr>`).join('');$('page-method').innerHTML=`<div class="guide"><div class="eyebrow">TRANSPARENT BY DESIGN</div><h1>Know what the model assumes.</h1><p class="sub">An exploratory simulator, not an employee prediction system.</p><h2>What is being simulated?</h2><p>One programme, four editable behavioural archetypes and a changing workforce across 3–24 months. Plan A and Plan B share the same workforce, random draws and programme; their support conditions differ. No AI service, MatrAIx, or model download is used.</p><h2>Audience and seniority</h2><p>All population, workload and completion charts now follow the selected course audience. Current associates only is a closed cohort fixed at the simulation start: later joiners do not enter the course or its charts, while departures can reduce the active cohort. New joiners only excludes the starting workforce. Historical completions are preserved.</p><p>Seniority is independent of archetype. Department mixes default to Not specified. Classroom effects default to zero and adjust only starting probability for instructor-led delivery. They are hypothetical, not inferred from job title. Actual classroom dates, seat limits and attendance are not modelled. Completion rates still use active assigned associates; leavers remain separately reported.</p><h2>What do the counts mean?</h2><p><strong>Active completion rate</strong> is completed active employees divided by active assigned employees at the selected month. The four stages are mutually exclusive current states. “Not assigned” covers people outside the audience or before launch. A dash means nobody is assigned.</p><p><strong>Completions to date</strong> retain employees who completed and later left. <strong>Left before finishing</strong> counts departures with an incomplete assignment. New joiners have their own assignment dates and deadlines. People can complete late; their detail shows this.</p><h2>Workforce changes</h2><p><strong>Simulated turnover to date</strong> is cumulative leavers divided by average monthly headcount across the selected period, multiplied by 100. Average headcount uses the mean of opening and closing headcount for each elapsed month. This is not annualised; a two-year value covers two years. Annual percentage inputs are separate assumptions.</p><p>Annual joiners are spread evenly, with fractional counts carried forward. Annual turnover is converted to a monthly departure probability: 1 − (1 − annual rate)^(1/12). Monthly overrides replace those estimates, and cannot remove more people than are present. Departures precede arrivals. Hiring and departure assumptions recur in year two.</p><p>Department archetype percentages set sampling probabilities, not exact quotas. This version does not model transfers, promotions, role-specific course eligibility, or correlations in departures.</p><h2>Learning time and competing requirements</h2><p>Mandatory hours are averages per employee. Completed year-to-date hours are subtracted in the first calendar year; the rest are distributed across the remaining months using the seasonal weights. Subsequent years receive the full annual requirement. New starters accrue their remaining months’ requirement plus onboarding hours.</p><p>Existing mandatory learning gets first use of capacity. Unfinished hours carry forward as a backlog. Remaining capacity is available to the proposed programme. Extra protected time is assumed to be genuinely additional. The proposed programme is excluded from existing mandatory totals to avoid double-counting.</p><h2>Behavioural rules</h2><p>Archetypes set monthly opening and starting probabilities, time engagement and manager responsiveness. Sponsorship adds 12 percentage points to opening probability. Manager encouragement adds 5 points to opening and the archetype’s manager effect to starting. Mandatory status adds 8 points to opening and 16 to starting.</p><p>Each relevance point above/below 3 changes starting and time engagement by 8 percentage points. Manager encouragement adds 10 points to time engagement; mandatory status adds 15. Rates are bounded at 2–98%. A seeded 0.75–1.25 effort multiplier produces individual variation. Programme progress uses remaining available hours × engagement × that multiplier. Modules are equal-sized and progress is derived from hours; this is not an assessment of learning or knowledge.</p><p><strong>These effects are assumptions, not causal findings.</strong> Changing the seed explores one source of variability; the app does not produce statistical confidence intervals.</p><h2>Historical reference</h2><p>These editable totals are retained for comparison and future calibration. They do not fit or validate the simulation. Use comparable programmes and matched time windows before interpreting differences.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Department</th><th>Invited</th><th>Started</th><th>Completed</th><th>Completed / invited</th></tr></thead><tbody>${rows}</tbody></table></div><h2>Storage and portability</h2><p>Your saved scenario stays in this browser profile on this local origin. Nothing is sent to an external service. Browser clearing or changing the address can make the saved scenario unavailable. Export scenario JSON for a durable backup and import it on another browser or device. Department CSV supports aggregate inputs; it does not import individual learning histories.</p><h2>What would make forecasts trustworthy?</h2><p>Historical course and cohort data, known launch conditions, explicit missing-data handling, and evaluation on held-out past programmes. Before using results for planning commitments, compare the model against a simple historical baseline and calibrate it. Do not use these illustrative outputs to assess individual employees.</p>${result.work.warnings.length?'<h2>Workforce adjustments in this run</h2><ul>'+result.work.warnings.map(w=>'<li>'+esc(w)+'</li>').join('')+'</ul>':''}</div>`;}
